==English==

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|en|inhability||disqualification for office}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|in|ability}}. Compare {{cog|frm|inhabilité}}, {{cog|ML.|inhabilitās}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɪnəˈbɪlɪti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-inability.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[lack|Lack]] of the [[ability]] to do something; [[incapability]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|26 November 2013|Daniel Taylor|Jack Wilshere scores twice to ease Arsenal to victory over Marseille|The Guardian|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2013/nov/26/arsenal-marseille-match-report-champions-league|text=The Premier League leaders did what many people thought was beyond them in their last European excursion, at the home of {{w|Borussia Dortmund}}, and they made light work of overcoming Marseille on a night when the one-sidedness was not reflected by their '''inability''' to add to {{w|Jack Wilshere}}'s two goals.}}
# Lack of the [[option]] to do something; [[powerlessness]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|unability}}

